● The culprit is in strokePetals (line 65). Because this version truncates each
  loop at petalDeg°, the end of one loop sits out on the petal while the next
  loop starts at the origin. At each petal boundary the code does moveTo(prevX, 
  prevY) — the previous point — and then lineTo the new point, so it draws a
  straight chord from the truncated loop tip back into the origin.

  The fix is to start the new sub-path at the new point instead of the previous
  one:

