● Done. The straight line into the origin came from the petal-boundary logic in
  strokePetals:

  - Each loop is truncated at petalDeg° (default 20°), so a loop's last point
    sits out on the petal while the next loop's first point is at the origin.
  - On a petal change, the code did moveTo(prevX, prevY) — i.e. it moved to the
    previous loop's end point — then lineTo to the next loop's origin point,
    which drew that chord back into the center.

  I changed it to moveTo(nx, ny) (the new point), so each new loop's sub-path
  starts fresh at the origin with no connecting line. The petals now render as
  separate arcs with no line running into the center, and the color transitions
  and Animate trace are unaffected.

